  "description": "League of Legends' dragons and Baron, on their own: with the game's own champions or with League of Legends Heroes / TFT heroes, no other mod needed (replaces the Workshop mod \"Elemental Drakes & Baron\": disable that one). The game's serpent becomes League's elemental drakes in League's order (two random, then the rift's element until the soul), each stack a felt team bonus (Infernal +8% attack damage and ability power, Mountain +10% armor and magic resist, Ocean 3% missing health every 5 s, Cloud +8% move speed, Hextech +10% attack speed and faster skills, Chemtech tenacity and life steal) in place of the game's small drake buff; the first team to four drakes claims the Dragon Soul (Infernal blasts, Mountain shield, Ocean healing, Cloud haste after the ultimate, Hextech chain lightning, Chemtech's last stand); every dragon after it is the Elder Dragon, whose takers burn enemy champions and execute them below 20% health for 90 s. Baron Nashor gives its takers the Hand of Baron for 120 s (+20% attack damage and ability power) and makes the minions near them take 40% less damage and hit 30% harder. Everything runs inside the simulation, the same in the server's pre-simulations and on screen; a state record on each nexus and a marker on the living dragon tell the screen what to draw. On screen: the game's own texts name them Baron Nashor and Elemental Drake (kill log, banners, results, graphs, encyclopedia, strategies), notices announce every drake by its element, the soul, the Elder Dragon, its executes and Baron, and a small HUD shows each team's drakes, soul and Elder / Baron time left; every trigger of a Dragon Soul, the soul taken, the Elder's burn and its execute play an effect on the battlefield (drawn by the mod itself). Draws the dragons' dense (high-definition) frames itself (the engine the League and TFT packs share). Writes a log for testing.",
  "last_updated": "2026-11-11",
  "mod_id": "league_dragons",
  "mod_type": "native",
  "name": "League Heroes: Dragons & Baron / 英雄联盟大小龙",
  "version": "0.4.3"
}
